     "page": 1,
     "text": "LLC Clinic\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Jason Rivera in consultation on August 13, 2025. The patient was referred for an evaluation of his valvular disease and murmur, which is of the mitral valve prolapse (MVP) type and is classified as mild. He is currently doing well with no need for medication to manage this condition.\n\nRegarding Mr. Rivera's cataracts, he reports no changes in his vision, and there have been no complications. He is currently under observation, with no medical treatment required at this time.\n\nAdditionally, Mr. Rivera has been managing his GERD (Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease) effectively. He has been on a regimen of pantoprazole 40 and omeprazole 40 mg, which he takes as prescribed. He reports a significant improvement in his symptoms and has been able to maintain good control of his acid reflux with these medications.\n\nDuring the visit, Mr. Rivera's blood pressure was recorded at 136/90, and his weight was 199 pounds. His physical examination was otherwise unremarkable, with normal findings in all systems reviewed.\n\nMr. Rivera's social history reveals that he is quite active, engaging in running 3 to 4 times per week. He also mentioned that his alcohol consumption is around three drinks per week. There is no documentation of tobacco use in his history.\n\nFamily history is pertinent for cardiovascular disease; Mr. Rivera's brother was diagnosed with coronary artery disease (CAD) at the age of 64, although he is still alive. Additionally, his father had Alzheimer's disease, which started at age 72, and unfortunately, he has since passed away.\n\nIn summary, Mr. Rivera's valvular disease/murmur, cataracts, and GERD are all currently under control. His lifestyle choices, including regular exercise and moderate alcohol consumption, are contributing positively to his overall health.\n\nThank you for referring Mr. Rivera to me for this evaluation. Please feel free to reach out if you have any further questions or need additional information.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Sabrina Sloan, MD\nFamily Medicine\nPorter LLC Clinic\n"
